{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1097171-how-many-per-city","id":1097171,"title":"How many per city?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-05-26T09:58:44-07:00","id":1097171,"title":"How many per city?","content":"So..after playing Bloodlines the Videogame. i keep with a perception that theres about 20 to 30 camarilla vamps per city, sabbat a bit more (maybe 60)<br /> but what about the others?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-26T10:46:25-07:00","id":1097176,"title":"","content":"A statement of 'there are X vampires per city' does...not work. It depensd on the size of the city, but that one's been chewed through countless times <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> I think the official statement was roughly 1 vamp per 100k mortals in a town, so 90 vampires in a city already assumes a huge city. Well, city and outskirts make it work, kind of.<br /> <br /> Still, while in modern times groups like the Sabbat and the Anarchs are really pushing that limit in some locations, I think Bloodlines simply had that many vampires because:<br /> Video game logic. It would be rather boring to only meet one vampire NPC every few miles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-26T15:02:43-07:00","id":1097313,"title":"","content":"i meant, waht about other supernaturals, kiths, mages, etc..","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-26T15:03:10-07:00","id":1097314,"title":"","content":"Well, there is a legitimate concern about how many Kindred can live in an area without detection. In general, you do not want more than 1% of the healthy adult human population to be fed upon every year because of the risk of hospitalization or death due to overfeeding. When you look at the USA, that means a ratio of around 1:50,000. Of course, animal blood can allow for greater populations (animal blood can allow up to a ratio of 1:10,000 for non-Ventrue). I generally run Kindred at a metropolitan average of 1:50,000, with animal blood providing large reserves of sustenance to supplement the luxury of human blood among non-Ventrue (Venture should always have Herd 4+ in my opinion unless they want to become dependent on Kindred blood).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-27T02:26:32-07:00","id":1097468,"title":"","content":"A few tentative ratios for cities by supernatural critter, mostly arrived at by looking solely at how many NPCs have been referred to in a locale - baseline 'bare minimums' to achieve the representation we see in the actual game world.<br /> <br /> <b>Mage</b><br /> San Francisco<b>: </b>Mages have 1:47,000 for the bay area as a whole and 1:5,400 if we use just San Francisco's population. Add the other supernaturals and the Bay Area ratio becomes 1:13,000. If they all met in the city one day, just because, San Francisco would temporarily have a ratio of 1:1500. <i>Let the freak flag fly</i>.<br /> Other mage ratios:<br /> -Richmond, VA at 1:19,500.<br /> -Prince Albert, Sasketchawan, at 1:3200.<br /> -Hong Kong, at 1:28,500.<br /> -Charleston, South Carolina at either 1:4800 or 1:33,250 for the greater metropolitan area.<br /> -Tryon, North Carolina at a terrifying 1:130. All Verbena. There are more verbena in that particular backwater than there are Asians or Native Americans.<br /> -Seattle, at 1:18,200.<br /> -Las Vegas, NV, is at 1:19,000. That book, ironically, gave us the mage figure of 1:150,000, while even at the greater municipal area the ratio is only 1:81,000. Of course, those ratios are averages, etc.<br /> -Greenland has 1:57,000.<br /> Paris is at a minimum figure of 1:650,000.<br /> The bare minimum global ratio, including mages we know nothing about or who live in the Umbra, is 1:842,500.<br /> <br /> <b>Changelings</b><br /> Philadelphia is at 1:252,000 people.<br /> Toronto is at 1:54,000.<br /> Hawaii rises higher to 1:38,500.<br /> San Francisco is higher still (noticing a pattern? If an Immortal Eyes novel or corebook was there, you get far better representation) at 1:16,500.<br /> But strangely, the highest ratio is not San Francisco, the glamour-vortex and attention hog. So far, it's Richmond California. Just outside of San Francisco itself, it outstrips that city in proportion by far. There is 1 changeling for every 3,350 normal people in that city.<br /> n America, there is a bare minimum of 1 Changeling to every 590,000 normal people.<br /> In the UK, it grows to 1:390,000.<br /> In Canada, it grows to 1:350,000.<br /> Great Britain as a whole moves lower, to 1:430,000 - and England alone is 1:420,000.<br /> Wales, however, is 1:89,000.<br /> Scotland is even higher, at 1:70,000.<br /> Ireland of course rises to a high of 1:52,000.<br /> Our bare minimum global ratio is around 1:2,810,000.<br /> <br /> <b>Demons</b><br /> We know very little here, and most places other than LA had maybe 1 demon referred to as in residence.<br /> At its height, LA had 1 demon for every 30,000 mortals in addition to its vampires, garou, mages, and changelings. It's a crowded city if you count the entire oWoD as one setting. Add just some of the vampires alone and you go to a 10,000:1 supernatural ratio. A real rough figure for LA, assuming all lines exist, comes out to around 400 supernatural creatures at its height - likely to be higher than that in real terms once I process all the entries. For a population ratio, that's 1:9,500. Turns out LA has a shitton of monsters. If we use the county figure though that drops to 1:30,000. Still pretty high, but not as dramatic.<br /> Paris has a minimum ratio of 1:10,000,000.<br /> <br /> <b>Imbued</b><br /> There is an absolute minimum of 1 Imbued (including Bystanders) for every 6 million people if we take the global figure, and 1:1.3mil if we extrapolate from the disproportionate American weighting of the Imbued population.<br /> <br /> <b>Vampire</b><br /> For St. Louis, if we wrap in the full greater area it's 1 vampire for every 96,000 mortals. The city alone drops that to 1:14,000. Add in ghouls and they respectively become 1:43,000 and 1:6,360. Toronto has 1:50,000 in the greater area with the local area dropping to 1:29,000. Sydney was at 1:82,500. San Diego was at 1:43,000. Stockholm, in an inversion of the ratios decreasing in modern sources, is terrifyingly low at 1:8,500.<br /> Paris was 1:40,600 Vampire+Ghoul:Human. 1:45,000 without ghouls.<br /> Mexico City sat at 1:42,500 Vamp:human in its first appearance, and an even higher 1:17,200 in its later appearance (1:14,500 with ghouls and revenants), and a bare minimum combined ratio of 1:12,300.<br /> Sarasota at the highest possible is 1:1,185 and at the lowest, 1:1,700 vampire:human. I know it's got a fair number of tourists going through but <i>jesus.</i> Tampa's not much better at 1:7,000. Disney World, bizarrely, is at 1:20,700 when you count the staff as the population, using the expy in a Darkling Plain.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Garou and Fera</b><br /> Like with Vampire, I haven't finished the data set for these guys.<br /> Paris has 1:10,000,000 with ratkin, but that means there's probably a ton more we just haven't seen yet.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-27T11:19:13-07:00","id":1097572,"title":"","content":"I have been to Tryon, NC (I used to live an hour from it), it is not cool enough to have that many Magee (especially Verbena).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-27T12:52:16-07:00","id":1097595,"title":"","content":"There's something like 30 million Elohim who took Lucifer's side, and I <i>think</i> I read somewhere that a third of those made it to the end of the war, meaning there's 10 million total Fallen.<br /> <br /> Which, when compared to the 666 Earthbound around back in the day, is not a very large percentage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12085-beriorn","name":"Beriorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12085_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-27T13:27:57-07:00","id":1097605,"title":"","content":"Is that canon in cWoD?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-27T13:51:27-07:00","id":1097614,"title":"","content":"All that's taken from the core Demon: The Fallen book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12085-beriorn","name":"Beriorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12085_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-27T15:15:13-07:00","id":1097624,"title":"","content":"The vast majority of those demons remain in the pit - and the number is more likely to be a poetic figure than a real one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-28T01:54:50-07:00","id":1097715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>loomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1097171-how-many-per-city?p=1097624#post1097624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The vast majority of those demons remain in the pit - and the number is more likely to be a poetic figure than a real one.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm willing to take the 100 million Elohim at face value, and we know that roughly a third of that rebelled. But from that point on it's anyone's guess: losses in the war, converts, demons who were destroyed in other ways, the ones who stuck around in the Shaodowlands... it can go anywhere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12085-beriorn","name":"Beriorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12085_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-28T03:24:10-07:00","id":1097726,"title":"","content":"The impression I get is their really aren't a gross amount of Imbued at all. They just have a really low life expectancy, most seem to die after a year of taking up the Reckoning, and they are quickly replaced by the messengers. So we could even have a couple Thousand Imbued, that regularly lose half their population.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-28T03:26:43-07:00","id":1097728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beriorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1097171-how-many-per-city?p=1097715#post1097715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm willing to take the 100 million Elohim at face value, and we know that roughly a third of that rebelled. But from that point on it's anyone's guess: losses in the war, converts, demons who were destroyed in other ways, the ones who stuck around in the Shaodowlands... it can go anywhere.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe almost a third again of the demons perished before the war was lost. It may have been Days of Fire that gave a number of 22 million or so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-28T03:39:16-07:00","id":1097733,"title":"","content":"Not quite. According to Days of Fire we began with 9,009,909 Angels. 3,003,302 rebelled, and 1,001,101 were killed. 2,002,204 were imprisoned.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-28T03:59:44-07:00","id":1097738,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>loomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1097171-how-many-per-city?p=1097733#post1097733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not quite. According to Days of Fire we began with 9,009,909 Angels. 3,003,302 rebelled, and 1,001,101 were killed. 2,002,204 were imprisoned.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yet the core rulebook hints at the number being at least 90 million. To be fair this mention comes from Gaviel, who is a Fallen whose memories may be a bit spotty, and the other coming from a document penned by Lucifer that's meant to both tell the truth and sound mystical.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12085-beriorn","name":"Beriorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12085_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-28T04:23:20-07:00","id":1097742,"title":"","content":"The number of rebels there is 33,300,030. I am inclined towards Lucifer's account, myself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-28T04:27:08-07:00","id":1097744,"title":"","content":"There's a transcript of a phonecall in Days of Fire where an unidentified Fallen calls itself &quot;one of the 2.002.204&quot;, which translates to two-thirds of the third mentioned at the start of Days of Fire. In either case it's a bit of an odd number.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12085-beriorn","name":"Beriorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12085_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-28T04:28:06-07:00","id":1097746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>loomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1097171-how-many-per-city?p=1097733#post1097733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not quite. According to Days of Fire we began with 9,009,909 Angels. 3,003,302 rebelled, and 1,001,101 were killed. 2,002,204 were imprisoned.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah that sounds more like it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-28T04:39:02-07:00","id":1097748,"title":"","content":"2,002,204 = 10 = 1.<br /> <br /> 2224. &quot;But we are all as an unclean <i>thing</i>, and all our righteousnesses <i>are</i> as filthy rags; and we all do fade as a leaf; and our iniquities, like the wind, have taken us away.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5307,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","user":"loomer","date":". 05-28-2017, 08:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-28T09:58:08-07:00","id":1097805,"title":"","content":"It does not matter how many fallen angels exist, it matters how many of them are on the Earth and need to be sent back on the quick train to the Abyss. While permanently killing them is difficult, they are probably not going to get too many second chances to come back before their superiors destroy them for their incompetence. It is not like there is enough room on Earth for another group of supernatural predators when we already have Ananasi, Changelings, Kindred, KJ, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","